  "id": "self-focus-v2-1a1c73367b",
  "term": "self-focus",
  "definition": "Self-focus, or self-focused attention, is the direction of attention toward oneself, often involving self-evaluation by comparing one’s current state with personal standards or desired states. In maladaptive forms, it can involve heightened attention to the self after negative events, with increased self-criticism and negative internal attributions.",
